                  "type": "specifications",
                  "content": "<h2>Top Force Transducer</h2>rnrn<p>20-275</p>rnrn<p><a href=\"https://pdiwebsitestorage.blob.core.windows.net/websitedocstorage/2026/03/Top-Force-Transducer_Technical-Spec-Sheet.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Top Force Transducer Technical Specifications</a></p>rnrn<p>Physical</p>rnrn<p><strong>The 1150</strong></p>rnrn<p>Weight: 254 Kg (560 lbs.)</p>rnrn<p>Height: 45.72 (18 in)</p>rnrn<p>Transducer Diameter: &nbsp;41cm (16 in)</p>rnrn<p>Plates Diameter: 50.8 cm (20 in)</p>rnrn<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>rnrn<p><strong>The 2400</strong></p>rnrn<p>Weight: 703 Kg (1550 lbs.)</p>rnrn<p>Height: 50.8 cm (20 in)</p>rnrn<p>Transducer Diameter: 61 cm (24 in)</p>rnrn<p>Plates Diameter: 76.2 cm (30 in)</p>rnrn<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>rnrn<p><strong>The 4000</strong></p>rnrn<p>Weight: 2177 Kg (4800 lbs.)</p>rnrn<p>Height: 76.2 cm (30 in)</p>rnrn<p>Transducer Diameter: 91 cm (36 in)</p>rnrn<p>Plates Diameter: 111.7 cm (44 in)</p>rnrn<p>Other</p>rnrn<p>Compatible with Pile Dynamics Analyzer &ndash; Dynamic Load Tester (PDA-DLT)<br />rnAccelerometers, Strain Transducers, and Averaging Cables sold separately<br />rnFull one-year warranty<br />rnSetup Guide provided in PDF form on a USB Drive</p>"
