                  "type": "description",
                  "content": "<h2>ConmaticMAX IMC, Electromechanical-Actuated, Soil Consolidation Machine Price in Bangladesh</h2>rnrn<p><strong>ConMatic IMC Soil Consolidation&nbsp;System</strong></p>rnrn<p>The HM-5480.3F ConMatic IMC machine is an automated controller for performing incremental, Constant Rate of Strain (CRS), and Swell&nbsp;tests.</p>rnrn<p><strong>The HM-5480.3F Includes:</strong></p>rnrn<ul>rn\t<li>NEXT Software HM-5100SW Consolidation-Specific&nbsp;Module</li>rn\t<li>Pancake Load cell</li>rn\t<li>Linear Strain Transducer</li>rn</ul>rnrn<p>Automated testing frees up technicians for other tasks and reduces man-power requirements of testing procedures by more than half. ConMatic IMC allows consolidation tests in the following modes of operation: constant load/stress, constant rate of loading, and constant rate of strain. One ConMatic IMC automated system can replace the production of several manual machines when&nbsp;performing:</p>rnrn<ul>rn\t<li>Incremental tests according to (ASTM D2435) Method B, where successive load increments are applied through 100% primary&nbsp;consolidation.</li>rn\t<li>Constant rate of strain (ASTM D4186) with controlled back&nbsp;pressure.</li>rn\t<li>Swell or collapse of soil (ASTM D4546) Method&nbsp;A/B.</li>rn</ul>rnrn<p>Once a sample has been placed onto the test platform and the test conditions set, the ConMatic IMC performs all consolidation tests, including moving to the next stress level, without operator assistance. The system automatically moves through the different test parameters specified by the user, with incremental consolidation tests typically being completed in 24 to 48 hours. Automated tests can be done with our NEXT PC software or without it if a PC is not&nbsp;available.</p>rnrn<p>The Humboldt NEXT software with the HM-5100SW Consolidation module uses sample deformation readings taken from the displacement transducer and load readings from the load cell to maintain a constant applied stress to the sample throughout the test. Testing data is recorded and displayed in real-time on the screen, while test data is stored and calculations are performed automatically. Humboldt&rsquo;s NEXT software with the HM-5100SW Consolidation module&nbsp;provides:</p>rnrn<ul>rn\t<li>Live test data tabulation and live graphing capabilities&nbsp;(real-time).</li>rn\t<li>Complete test reporting, including all calculations and graphs required for&nbsp;testing.</li>rn\t<li>Review and export of tests using Microsoft Excel (CSV)&nbsp;format.</li>rn\t<li>Smart Test Function: automatically picks up where it left off if the test was not finished due to unexpected&nbsp;events.</li>rn</ul>rnrn<p>The unique design of the ConMatic IMC system enables the user to connect multiple ConMatic IMC units to a single computer when connected via a LAN-network. Computer Control NEXT software and the enhanced Consolidation module, HM-5100SW, are included with the ConMatic IMC automated machine. This software provides robust machine control, data acquisition and report generation for those using a computer to control testing operations. In addition, operators have the ability to view and control testing operations from the controlling PC, while also providing report generating capabilities using the test-specific software module. Whether you are controlling a single or multiple machines, the HM-5475.3F ConMatic IMC, machine, in conjunction with the NEXT testing software, provides a complete solution for the acquisition, recording, and presentation of testing data in data tabulation and graphic chart formats with the&nbsp;following:</p>rnrn<ul>rn\t<li>Machine control, and data acquisition via a networked&nbsp;computer.</li>rn\t<li>Provides the ability to use Humboldt&lsquo;s Next Software&rsquo;s advanced test-specific&nbsp;modules.</li>rn\t<li>Real-time graph chart, and numerical display of tests via computer&nbsp;display.</li>rn\t<li>Effective sampling rate up to 50 readings per&nbsp;second.</li>rn\t<li>Stores unlimited tests with up to 3000 points per&nbsp;test.</li>rn\t<li>Up to 255 individual tests can be run simultaneously from a single&nbsp;PC.</li>rn\t<li>Provides advanced graphing&nbsp;capabilities.</li>rn\t<li>Provides full-unit customization.</li>rn\t<li>Reports can be exported to Excel or a CSV file, if desired, and Humboldt can provide custom integration/export solutions for LIMS, EQuIS, gINT, as&nbsp;well.</li>rn\t<li>Stand-Alone reports are available in Excel (CSV)&nbsp;format</li>rn</ul>rnrn<p>The unique design of the ConMatic IMC system enables the user to connect multiple ConMatic IMC units to a single computer when connected via a&nbsp;LAN-network.</p>rnrn<p><strong>Computer Control</strong><br />rnNEXT software and the enhanced Consolidation module, HM-5100SW, are included with the ConMatic IMC automated machine. This software provides robust machine control, calibration, data acquisition and report generation for those using a computer to control testing operations. In addition, operators have the ability to view and control testing operations from the controlling PC, while also providing report generating capabilities using the test-specific software module. Whether you are controlling a single, or multiple machines, the HM-5475.3F machine, in conjunction with the NEXT testing software, provides a complete solution for the acquisition, recording and presentation of testing data in data tabulation and graphic chart formats with the&nbsp;following:</p>rnrn<ul>rn\t<li>Machine control, and data acquisition via a networked&nbsp;computer.</li>rn\t<li>Provides the ability to use Humboldt&rsquo;s Next Software&rsquo;s advanced test-specific&nbsp;modules.</li>rn\t<li>Real-time graphs, charts, and numerical display of tests via computer&nbsp;display.</li>rn\t<li>Effective sampling rate up to 50 readings per&nbsp;second.</li>rn\t<li>Stores unlimited tests with up to 3000 points per&nbsp;test.</li>rn\t<li>Up to 255 individual tests can be run simultaneously from a single&nbsp;PC.</li>rn\t<li>Provides advanced graphing&nbsp;capabilities.</li>rn\t<li>Provides full-unit customization.</li>rn\t<li>Reports can be exported to Excel or a CSV file, if desired, and Humboldt can provide custom integration/export solutions for LIMS, EQuIS, gINT, as&nbsp;well.</li>rn\t<li>Stand-Alone reports are available in Excel (CSV)&nbsp;format.</li>rn</ul>"
